1
00:00:01,383 --> 00:00:03,504
-Hi, Beto.
-What's up?

2
00:00:05,199 --> 00:00:06,963
-How are you?
-Not so good.

3
00:00:06,996 --> 00:00:09,496
I've been here for 5min,
and no one came.

4
00:00:10,177 --> 00:00:11,860
But it's full of waiters.

5
00:00:11,893 --> 00:00:16,072
-Yes, but look. Hey, buddy!
-What are you doing?

6
00:00:16,105 --> 00:00:18,521
You touched his arm?
You're not in the subway.

7
00:00:18,554 --> 00:00:20,330
There's a way
to approach them.

8
00:00:20,363 --> 00:00:23,279
Approach them?
I want a beer. It's their job.

9
00:00:23,312 --> 00:00:26,296
-Hey, buddy!
-Don't talk like that to Toño.

10
00:00:26,329 --> 00:00:27,789
His name is Toño?

11
00:00:27,822 --> 00:00:29,918
-Toño, come here, please.
-No, stop.

12
00:00:29,951 --> 00:00:31,999
Toño likes to be won over.

13
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:33,995
Won over? How?

14
00:00:34,028 --> 00:00:36,396
-Make him jealous?
-How will I do that?

15
00:00:36,429 --> 00:00:38,735
With Sergio,
the waiter with the beard.

16
00:00:38,768 --> 00:00:40,623
Toño is jealous of Sergio.

17
00:00:40,656 --> 00:00:44,336
Say something nice about him.
Suck up to him, go for it.

18
00:00:44,457 --> 00:00:45,541
Okay.

19
00:00:46,959 --> 00:00:50,773
-Sergio is the best waiter here.
-Yes, the best.

20
00:00:52,097 --> 00:00:53,460
It's working, see?

21
00:00:56,114 --> 00:01:00,936
I read in a magazine that Sergio
is the best waiter in Mexico.

22
00:01:01,817 --> 00:01:03,718
Sergio, can I have a beer?

23
00:01:03,751 --> 00:01:06,484
What are you doing?
That's cheating.

24
00:01:06,837 --> 00:01:08,526
You've got Toño.

25
00:01:08,559 --> 00:01:11,438
Pretend you're ignoring him,
that you can't see him.

26
00:01:12,088 --> 00:01:14,513
I've never seen Toño
so crazy for someone.

27
00:01:14,553 --> 00:01:17,592
What? I don't understand.
What should I do?

28
00:01:17,625 --> 00:01:21,268
Take the menu.
Take it and look at him.

29
00:01:21,301 --> 00:01:23,687
Look at him slowly.
Seduce him.

30
00:01:25,019 --> 00:01:27,716
Look at him as if you'll order
something expensive.

31
00:01:27,749 --> 00:01:30,098
What is it?
Shellfish? Crawfish?

32
00:01:30,131 --> 00:01:32,804
What is it?
Look at the menu then at him.

33
00:01:32,837 --> 00:01:37,514
Now we'll do something risky.
You'll raise your hand. Raise it.

34
00:01:38,639 --> 00:01:40,251
Raise your hand slowly.

35
00:01:40,557 --> 00:01:42,663
Slowly. Now call him.

36
00:01:43,699 --> 00:01:45,866
That's it. Act naturally.

37
00:01:48,961 --> 00:01:50,810
-Hello.
-Hello.

38
00:01:51,292 --> 00:01:53,209
-What's your name, sir?
-Toño.

39
00:01:53,242 --> 00:01:54,408
Toño.

40
00:01:55,372 --> 00:01:56,771
Toño?

41
00:01:57,308 --> 00:02:00,133
Are you from here?
You sound from Colonia Doctores.

42
00:02:00,166 --> 00:02:02,814
-No, I'm from Obrera.
-Beautiful!

43
00:02:02,847 --> 00:02:04,841
I go there a lot.

44
00:02:06,837 --> 00:02:08,970
-Can I be less formal?
-Yes, of course.

45
00:02:09,466 --> 00:02:11,971
Toño, what do you like
to drink?

46
00:02:14,490 --> 00:02:15,808
Juice.

47
00:02:16,227 --> 00:02:17,678
-Juice?
-Yes.

48
00:02:18,302 --> 00:02:19,726
Delicious.

49
00:02:21,105 --> 00:02:23,838
But, for example,
if you were in a bar.

50
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:29,049
Well, in this case, beer.
I really like beer.

51
00:02:29,082 --> 00:02:31,773
-I drink a lot of beer.
-What a coincidence!

52
00:02:31,806 --> 00:02:33,985
We love beer too.

53
00:02:34,591 --> 00:02:36,968
Listen, Toño dear...

54
00:02:38,035 --> 00:02:41,461
If you happen to pass by the bar -
no pressure -,

55
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:44,315
could you maybe bring us
a couple of beers?

56
00:02:44,390 --> 00:02:45,739
Any beer?

57
00:02:46,387 --> 00:02:48,309
-Well, preferably...
-Yes.

58
00:02:48,672 --> 00:02:51,352
-Yes, any beer. Okay.
-Yes, of course.

59
00:02:51,386 --> 00:02:52,839
-Thanks.
-Sure.

60
00:02:54,909 --> 00:02:56,314
Well done!

61
00:02:57,991 --> 00:03:00,984
What an idiot!
I forgot to order food.

62
00:03:01,017 --> 00:03:04,005
Don't worry.
They'll send chicken fried steak.

63
00:03:04,038 --> 00:03:05,124
How?

64
00:03:05,157 --> 00:03:07,549
My match on Tinder
is Rubén, the chef.

65
00:03:07,582 --> 00:03:10,230
-Dude!
-I'm a dog!

66
00:03:17,294 --> 00:03:19,324
It didn't work with Toño.

67
00:03:19,372 --> 00:03:22,739
No, you should try Leo,
he's a man whore.

68
00:03:22,772 --> 00:03:25,267
He swaps sides
whenever you ask.

69
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,417
-You can tip him anywhere.
-Leo!

70
00:03:28,439 --> 00:03:30,333
-Leo!
-Leo!